&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, Employee Relations&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;San Mateo, CA (hybrid) -&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;requires 2 days in the office&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Role Overview:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;We are seeking a strategic, influential, and forward‑thinking Senior Manager to lead our People Experience (PX) function for the AMER region. This role is responsible for driving high‑quality HR Generalist delivery, shaping Employee Relations strategy, and orchestrating complex organizational change across a dynamic, global matrix environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;This role directly manages both the &lt;strong&gt;AMER HR Generalist (PXC) team&lt;/strong&gt; and the &lt;strong&gt;AMER Employee Relations (ER) team&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring cohesive service delivery, operational excellence, and a consistent employee experience across the region. You will guide both teams through annual HR cycles, coach them through change, and elevate their impact through data‑driven insights, process improvements, and strong stakeholder partnerships.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;While day‑to‑day work is rooted in AMER operations, this role also plays a critical part in aligning complex regional practices with the global PX organization. You will collaborate closely with HR Business Partners, Legal, Studio HR, and global PX leaders to deliver integrated solutions, influence cross‑regional initiatives, and contribute to the evolution of our global HR operating model.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Success in this role requires exceptional communication, a proactive mindset, strong analytical capability, and the ability to navigate ambiguity while balancing strategic thinking with hands‑on execution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Strategic HR Organizational Change Orchestration &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Partner with HRBPs, Legal, and senior leaders to assess, map, lead, and implement AMER organizational change. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the assessment of timelines, processes, interconnectivity with other HR teams, and creation of change plans. Ensure timely execution with effective communication, stakeholder management, creative problem-solving, and curiosity to improve internal ways of working. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deploy high-quality content for various audiences, including leadership communication, presentations, training material, and management information reports.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the PX AMER Senior Director with team design, measurement and development and execution of a full and robust roadmap of HR Generalist (PXC) &amp;amp; AMER ER projects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize business information and build positive relationships with HRBPs and leadership teams to identify insights, make recommendations and decisions as appropriate. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an active member of the PX Global Leadership Team (PXLT)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Collaboration, Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Team Management &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Establish trust and influence senior stakeholders while navigating uncertainty. Ability to ‘cut through the noise’ and identify high vs low impact activity, risk, and advise the business and wider People team with data and best practice  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with HR Business Partners, Legal, Studio HR and other global stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor the HR Generalist (PXC) team and Employee Relations (ER) team to provide high-quality support and cultivate an agile, collaborative, and dedicated culture. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong connections with diverse stakeholders across various time zones with diverse project demands. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Employee Relations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with Legal on ER matters and employment law.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage complex ER matters with potential reputational/legal risk in conjunction with Legal and the ER specialists. Oversee all AMER ER cases and drive operational efficiency in processes  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive system adoption and cohesive usage to establish consistent metrics and measurement of ER issues in region. Partner with HRBP’s to present and analyse data to shift from reactive to proactive Employee Relations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the global PX team to align on system use, processes and ER cadence.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver complex OD actions with HR Generalist and ER teams.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;A proven senior HR manager with extensive ER and HRBP experience in a matrixed, complex, global environment.  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years management experience of leading teams at HR Generalist (PXC) and ER specialist level. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of influencing senior collaborators and delivering strategic HR initiatives. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process mapping, evaluation and system thinking mindset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High levels of data literacy and insight development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and influencing skills at all levels. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to think strategically and act operationally with a proactive, forward-looking perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with data driven impact analysis &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial cultural Change Management and HR project experience &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating ambiguity with strong problem-solving, analytical, and innovative influencing skills. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial competence with a people-first, efficiency, and compliance-conscious approach. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-SF1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At SIE, we consider several factors when setting each role’s base pay range, including the competitive benchmarking data for the market and geographic location.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the base pay range may vary in line with our hybrid working policy and individual base pay will be determined based on job-related factors which may include knowledge, skills, experience, and location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, this role &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;is eligible&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; for SIE’s top-tier benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, matching 401(k), paid time off, wellness program and coveted employee discounts for Sony products. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This role also may be eligible for a bonus package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Click&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.playstation.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to learn more.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The estimated base pay range for this role is listed below.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$185,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$277,600 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
